{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1452221-the-makara-and-the-plain","id":1452221,"title":"The Makara and The Plain","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-14T13:40:09-07:00","id":1452221,"title":"The Makara and The Plain","content":"So, we have questions on this subject, the other two have proven to be interesting conversation pieces, the Makara is a great case of where the physical and the metaphorical intertwine, and it's the last one I have fully written up. This one gets rambly, and those of you were around here in July 2019 might be able to notice a certain conversation on my mind, but with that said, let's look at the Makara and the Plain. <hr /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Makara, Nightmares of the Depths</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It\u2019s the drowning that gets you, right? That\u2019s always what you think about when it comes to the dangers of water-the desperate attempt to cage the air in your lungs and it\u2019s just as panicked and inevitable flight from your body if you\u2019re left under for too long.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The water\u2019s more of a threat than that though-it\u2019s inherent, you can feel it when you start to surround yourself with it. You aren\u2019t built for it. Your limbs don\u2019t work for it, and the way you orient yourself is so easily lost when motion becomes a three dimensional affair. There\u2019s always that panic, that you don\u2019t know which way is up, the moment when you stop moving, and your only hope is that when you look up, you see light and not the darkness. You dive in and move in this world, and you learn that you don\u2019t belong there. You also know it when you meet any of the inhabitants of the water, because it\u2019s </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>so easy</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> for them, to move around, to breathe, to keep purchase and cool, to just go at you, because this is their world-they know it like the back of their fins and tentacles, like a familiar itch in their teeth. We know more about the reaches of space and bacteria on moons than we do our own oceans</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There\u2019s an alien world that we can barely comprehend under that surface of stuff we just drink for survival.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">That\u2019s the other physical catch-we know there\u2019s dangers plenty, both on and in the water. Rivers and lakes and oceans are all hungry, and we shouldn\u2019t dare to deal with them, but we need to drink water to survive, need to cross it to travel, need to plumb the depths for food and resources. We can\u2019t escape those dangers because there\u2019s too much that calls to us.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mermaids are a great transition from the physical to the abstract. Our physical fears all stem from the real, but the allure is all sex and sexuality, of companionship for pride or for lonelieness, for something more. It\u2019s our fear of that sex and sexuality, of our carnal desires, that makes the mermaid a leviathan in her own right.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">And so it goes. The world is filled with surfaces, and complex, strange worlds beneath them-hell, we may not even fully comprehend our own selves, questioning our sex, our gender, our profession, our friendships, our choices, our identities. People don\u2019t dive into politics or religion because a little bit of swimming reveals deep worlds with more complexity than we thought to them. There\u2019s always some kind of thing going on that has more people and activity going on with it than you realize, and sometimes you just need to pull back to that placid surface because it makes sense. We don\u2019t look too closely at a lot of things, from the leather whip in our grandma\u2019s room to the racism going on in our nations to our own hearts desire, because diving in deep reveals how complex and hard a lot of what we thought we knew really was.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">At the heart of it, the fear of the depths is to confront our own inability to </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>handle complexity and unknown factors</i></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, our likelihood at failing to </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>adapt</i></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> to a world more nuanced and alien than we ever thought. It\u2019s that fear </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>we\u2019ll never really get it all.</i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>And that\u2019s all right</i></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Truth be told, there\u2019s too much in the world to ever be free from our own ignorance and failure to comprehend. There\u2019s going to be times we end up in over our heads, and that\u2019ll cost us, and being aware of that failing is going to get us a lot further along in the problem than trying to pretend it won\u2019t happen. It\u2019s okay to be afraid that things are going to be more complicated than we can understand. It\u2019s okay to admit that we\u2019re going to get it wrong going forward. We\u2019ll lose our way, we\u2019ll get hurt, and we may even drown.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It\u2019s also important to understand the fear of wanting things we don\u2019t fully comprehend, because sometimes that means we have things about ourselves we need to come to terms. If our sense of want and need lead to harm or self-destruction, then it\u2019s important to learn to respect that comes from somewhere, that we sort out what is merely other fears tying into the desire, and which belies problems and issues that we need to sort out and pay attention to.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It\u2019s important, then, in this sense, to hold our breath in these matters, a metaphor that means a whole lot. On the physical level, we learn to survive in the water by carrying more and more air with us, by learning how to regulate our pressure, to keep as much as possible and use as little as possible. In the abstract, it means learning to talk and assert less, and to listen more, to pay attention more, to take in whatever we\u2019re coming at.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This stillness and calm relays into the needs of orientation and learning to go with the flow as well. When you find yourself disoriented and deep underwater, letting one\u2019s self float will tend to orient your legs downward, as the lower part of your body tends to be heavier than your upper half, thus telling you where the surface is. Floating in social situations where you don\u2019t know what\u2019s going on, going with the flow of things, will lead you at least get the form of how things are done, if not reveal the environmental reasons they are done with time. Learning to go in and take your cues from others and the world around you begins to reveal more information from that.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Finally, you develop a careful but sinuous power to pushing through the environment, learn that it\u2019s just applying your strength but twisting your form through the thicker medium. In society, you learn how to carefully apply power and push against it as well as slip into it, learning where audacity and discretion come into play in kind. You learn to carefully touch the edges of things so as to not be ripped away or stung, and then to reach out and grab onto those things that are of benefit to you, be it the food of the day, or the heart of a coworker or the praise of a general. You can push against the system and emerge more powerful for it, because you have read the currents and know how to play them to your strengths. You\u2019ll meet with others when you breach the surface and confound them with your strange, new alien knowledge and strength, as alluring in your power and confidence as you are confounding in your new complexities.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Forsworn of the Depths, the Plain</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Stop me if you\u2019ve heard this one: \u201cYou\u2019re overthinking it.\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Plain don\u2019t need to fear complexity because things aren\u2019t really that complex. There\u2019s no hidden nuances to society, there\u2019s just people who want to get more out of the program than not. There\u2019s no subtleties in human behavior-if you dress like that, it\u2019s because you\u2019re asking for it, admit it or not. Politics? Not that hard, people just can\u2019t handle democracy. Religion? What to it, Jesus saves. What\u2019s all this stuff about the Jews, my friend was a Jew and he never had these problems. You get the idea.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Plain reduce the world to operating on a handful of simple principles, often ones that are affirmed by their own life experiences-and so tend to reinforce their own lifestyles and experiences while devaluing others. Other people just want to make it complicated because they don\u2019t have any common sense, just aren\u2019t able to read the room, because they can\u2019t handle the simple facts. People are going for an angle. They don\u2019t need nuance and an ability to read the room and parsing out what\u2019s true or not when they\u2019ve got the facts all ready inside themselves-knowing the facts beats getting to know the circumstances and details any day of the week. The Plain see things as they are, and suffocate everyone else in the shallow end for disagreeing.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">To their credit, the Plain do tend to play towards practical simplicities rather than nonsensical ones-if it doesn\u2019t bear the plausibility of truth, then it\u2019s not a plain and simple truth. They\u2019re very matter of fact and their principles do tend to work in their sphere-but their rejection of other\u2019s points of views that complicate affairs and insistence that they already know the answer to situations can cause them problems when they\u2019re thrown in the deep end. When that happens, the simple principles are played to their extreme-if killing it won\u2019t do, overkill will, and you use booms when bangs are falling short. The backfire effect ignites when contradictions come into contact with the core beliefs of the Plain, and so long as their beliefs can be validated in some kind of way. Messier victories as a result of that don\u2019t cause the Plain to question it, as it still proves they knew how things were all along.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Far more complicated with the Plain is that their tendency to reduce and simplify </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>don\u2019t</i></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> stop them from adding in new principles, and so attempts to show them how things really are and conveying a sense of nuance can seem like it\u2019s going swimmingly until the Plain reveal an insultingly truncated form of the lessons taught. It takes nuance and care to guide the Plain into a situation where newer conceptions of reality force them to really ask questions about their core beliefs about how things work and admit that something might be more than they can comprehend right now, and embrace that simplest and ultimate truth before they can really heal and learn from their fear. Still, because of this, the Plain can be the friendliest of the Forsworn, and seemingly the most likely to renounce their heroic journey, since their rejection still leads to building new outlooks. The corpses of thousands of hopeful Leviathans build the ziggurat of ignorance the Plain exist in, of course.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T14:11:11-07:00","id":1452229,"title":"","content":"BTW, if you want a great read for the Makara based on this, check out the chapter from Gunnerkrigg Court, <a href=\"https://www.gunnerkrigg.com/?p=2270\" target=\"_blank\">She Gave Us An Ocean</a>. Even if yer not familiar with the story so far, it'll make sense enough on it's own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T14:23:18-07:00","id":1452230,"title":"","content":"This is me, 100% not surprised by a Gunnerkrigg recommendation XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T14:23:36-07:00","id":1452231,"title":"","content":"Um. Well.<br /> <br /> It's a powerful piece of writing, but ... after reading it, and your version of Eshmaki, I still find it hard to see the line between them. It looks as if, to decide whether a Beast is an Eshmaki or a Makara, the only thing to go on is &quot;is this a land-based monster or a sea-based one?&quot; The basic fear in both cases is of ignorance and inscrutability. It's just that the Makara are a fear of ignorance of things you've already met, while Eshmaki are less specific.<br /> <br /> The Bright and the Plain are just as hard to distinguish - both are obsessed with defining, categorizing, and limiting, the Plain are just ... less inclined to test their theories when they think they've found the answer? Or are the Bright the arrogant scientist brandishing his credentials, while the Plain is the man on the street, sheltering in conventional wisdom?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T14:58:05-07:00","id":1452240,"title":"","content":"The Bright is obsessed with always knowing more because he thinks knowing things will make him feel secure, the Plain thinks there's nothing more to know, so he'll lump everything together into pre-defined concepts.<br /> <br /> The Bright is on a quest that he himself knows will never end, the more he knows the more there is to know, he is definitely the mad scientist type.<br /> How can he be a villain? One word: dissection.<br /> There's an inherent destruction in the process of knowing, specially when that applies to humans, thinking as them as nothing more than a machine that can be understood by analyzing their physical processes is basically dehumanizing them. Things can be more than the sum of its parts. You can definitely know LESS about something the more you study it, the Eshmaki will make you remember that.<br /> <br /> The Plain is much simpler, he looks at the Bright and calls him a deluded fool, he is right, but he answers that not by acknowledging that he just can't know everything, he answers that by saying &quot;you already know everything there is to know, you are just overthinking&quot;. But you don't really know everything, and sometimes the unknown has teeth, the Makara will remind you of that.<br /> <br /> Both can't deal with the fact there will always be unknowns, but they answer it in very different ways.<br /> <br /> By the way, the overlap is in Eshmaki and Makaras, it's already there in the original, not in the Forsworn. This is so good exactly because it makes them differ more by having them inverted in different ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26086,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26086-dreadqueen","user":"DreadQueen","date":". 06-14-2021, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26086-dreadqueen","name":"DreadQueen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T15:09:28-07:00","id":1452242,"title":"","content":"The Plain takes the Fear of the Depths and says &quot;there's no abyss to be afraid of, no horror lurking beneath us, no unknown secret minds cannot bear to know. What exists is what you can see. Here, in the open, clear and plain, without any room for nuance or deviancy.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T15:35:32-07:00","id":1452245,"title":"","content":"For me, what the Makara are was really solidified by a great video essay by Jacob Geller, all about humanity's fear of, well, the depths. It focused more on caves than the ocean, but those are a Makara thing, too. If I can figure out how to embed a video, maybe I'll post it later.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the video's main idea is the scariest bit about the depths isn't so much that we don't know what's down there, or even that we don't belong there; it is the <i>fascination</i>. People always come back to deep, dark places. We cannot resist the alien allure of a cave, a lake, or the sea. I think Arc's write-up here gets at the same idea, or at least close to it, albeit in a round-about, rambley way.<br /> <br /> So, to me, the Makara are the fear of getting lost, or losing yourself, in an alien environment. And the scariest part is, you are only there because <i>you</i> took that risk. You went into the cave, you got on the boat, you went out of your depth. You chose to put yourself near or across a boundary. And the other world was not meant for you. If you survive... you'll probably do it again, whether for the thrill or the rewards. The Makara are alluring sirens and hypnotic angler fish just as much as they are hulking krakens and miles-long sea serpents.<br /> <br /> If you want to simplify it even more, you might say that the Makara are a fear of risk. That they are the anxiety of putting yourself in danger, expressed through the lens of inappropriate environments [their Lairs are the most likely to be hostile to humanity], but I think that ends up confusing them more. Regardless, I think this interpretation is more adjacent to the Eshmaki's unknown, rather than truly overlapping with it. Like two ships passing in the dark of night, or two people sharing a bed. Close, maybe even related, but distinct.<br /> <br /> Just my two cents on the subject. I think the Makara have always been a weird one to plainly ascribe a &quot;fear&quot; to [even if the book has no trouble leaving it at &quot;the depths&quot;]. Like, it's easy to sorta understand that, but without being able to really put it in words, y'know?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T16:04:47-07:00","id":1452248,"title":"","content":"Could it be simplified to Eshmaki = &quot;Fear of not knowing&quot; and Makara = &quot;Fear of knowing&quot; then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26086-dreadqueen","name":"DreadQueen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T16:18:24-07:00","id":1452249,"title":"","content":"So, a Makara is a monster you have to make a special effort to meet, and the fear that, by making that effort, you won't be able to get back. While an Eshmaki is a monster that might decide to hunt you down, and the fear of being surprised, suddenly in danger. Which is why Makara have Alien Allure, and Eshmaki have From the Shadows.<br /> <br /> And the Bright reject the idea that they can be caught by surprise, being sure that they can learn enough about anything to predict its actions. While the Plain refuse to go beyond what they know, or to admit any attraction or value to the mysterious.<br /> <br /> OK, I can see that as a viable distinction. You'd need to revise both writeups to bring it out properly, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-14T21:28:03-07:00","id":1452274,"title":"","content":"I got to this too late in the day to address a lot of points, but I did have a thought from earlier about a way to think about the Plain (and the implied contrast to, say, the Enlightened).<br /> <br /> On the one hand, Jim from Blazing Saddles once said of the Plain &quot;You've got to remember that these are just simple farmers. These are people of the land. The common clay of the new West. You know... morons.&quot;<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Alexander the Pretty Alright was channeling some pretty strong Plain energy when he decided he was gonna ruin an oracles day by solving that knot problem.<br /> <br /> Sometimes the simplest solution is the best one. Othertimes, it's treating every problem like a nail, because why would you use anything but a hammer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-15T05:51:29-07:00","id":1452309,"title":"","content":"So I've just emerged from my Exalted phase in order to say that all of those articles are very, very cool. While I get why 2e have generally turned the antagonists into more simplified in terms of system and narrative, I really like seeing it, and modeling the narrative for different forms of Heroism as dark mirrors to the Families is a very cool concept.<br /> <br /> *quietly returning to my Exalted projects*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T11:15:31-07:00","id":1452658,"title":"","content":"Just popping in to say that I am thoroughly enjoying these write ups. You do a great job of exploring problematic worldviews without casting them as irredeemable. I am quite interested in what your takes on the Ugallu and Inguma would look like. <br /> <br /> I can\u2019t say I\u2019m 100% in love with the model of Heroes as essentially failed Beasts (I prefer a model where they are separate, equally dysfunctional aspects of the human psycho-immune system), but I do concede that the parallels it lets you draw between the Families and their Heroic counterparts are an excellent basis of reframing the problematic elements of the game. I particularly like the vibe that Hunger isn\u2019t completely parasitic, and is more about the Beast wanting to share this catharsis they went through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T11:43:06-07:00","id":1452660,"title":"","content":"This is really good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-17T21:37:49-07:00","id":1452737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1452221-the-makara-and-the-plain?p=1452658#post1452658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just popping in to say that I am thoroughly enjoying these write ups. You do a great job of exploring problematic worldviews without casting them as irredeemable. I am quite interested in what your takes on the Ugallu and Inguma would look like.<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t say I\u2019m 100% in love with the model of Heroes as essentially failed Beasts (I prefer a model where they are separate, equally dysfunctional aspects of the human psycho-immune system), but I do concede that the parallels it lets you draw between the Families and their Heroic counterparts are an excellent basis of reframing the problematic elements of the game. I particularly like the vibe that Hunger isn\u2019t completely parasitic, and is more about the Beast wanting to share this catharsis they went through.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the end model is going to be directly Heroes as failed Beasts-I don't think of it like that, in fact in a move I would never slip in as anything other than a rumor or legend to play with, I tend to make them the first &quot;response&quot;* to the Insatiable-so much as I think they are just one of the three main lines of Children the Dark Mother had, alongside the Insatiable and Beasts. They just happen to have more particular relationship with how one of these other Children comes about versus that other one that completely skips past the normal process.<br /> <br /> As for Hunger.....well, on the one hand, I did really want to explore how the elements of Beast could be positive, and they are all interconnected. On the other hand....Hunger is it's own show.<br /> <br /> *in as much as I want to emphasize the Dark Mother having Children for reasons, which I don't know how much I want to think like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T08:27:38-07:00","id":1452782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1452221-the-makara-and-the-plain?p=1452737#post1452737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the end model is going to be directly Heroes as failed Beasts-I don't think of it like that, in fact in a move I would never slip in as anything other than a rumor or legend to play with, I tend to make them the first &amp;quot;response&amp;quot;* to the Insatiable-so much as I think they are just one of the three main lines of Children the Dark Mother had, alongside the Insatiable and Beasts. They just happen to have more particular relationship with how one of these other Children comes about versus that other one that completely skips past the normal process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, that works. That makes Heroes the Children closest to humanity, with Insatiables being that farthest, and Beasts being in the middle. All related, but distinct by where they stand in relation to the Tenemos. <br /> <br /> To over extend the metaphor: Insatiables are the angsty older sibling who complains that no ones understands them. Heroes are the spoiled youngest who demands everything revolves around them. And Beasts are the besieged middle child who wishes everyone would stop killing each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-18T08:37:52-07:00","id":1452786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1452221-the-makara-and-the-plain?p=1452782#post1452782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ooh, that works. That makes Heroes the Children closest to humanity, with Insatiables being that farthest, and Beasts being in the middle. All related, but distinct by where they stand in relation to the Tenemos.<br /> <br /> To over extend the metaphor: Insatiables are the angsty older sibling who complains that no ones understands them. Heroes are the spoiled youngest who demands everything revolves around them. And Beasts are the besieged middle child who wishes everyone would stop killing each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>....Yes, I had actually intended that arrangement of the Children in regards to the depths of the Dreaming and didn't accidentally set that up.<br /> <br /> I do like oldest, middle and youngest arrangement, though in my books the reason I stopped calling Beasts the Eldest is that they're the <i>youngest</i> in my mind. But again, this is something we wouldn't declare a canonical answer for/to.<br /> <br /> Also they embody the three main takes on Nihilism, that one <i>very</i> deliberately so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-25T20:21:01-07:00","id":1453508,"title":"","content":"Fun Makara-adjacent fact: Before he was a psychoanalyst, Freud was a marine biologist (his obsession was eel testicles).<br /> <br /> All this has been really exhilarating, thought-provoking stuff. I look forward to what ultimately emerges from the depths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-26T12:52:51-07:00","id":1453589,"title":"","content":"I really like how you wrote this up. Personally I've never had the issue, but I know plenty of people who've had trouble with the overlap makara and eshmaki have, It makes me look forward to your writeup on the talassi (where I had slight trouble understanding the difference between them and the anakim), and I think I know here you're going with them and the libertines.<br /> <br /> Also love how the Plain and the Enlightened are basically opposites","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-30T15:09:35-07:00","id":1453869,"title":"","content":"ok, am i the only one who sees one of those right wing nuts who buy trumps lies as an archtypical example of the plain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-30T15:22:53-07:00","id":1453871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1452221-the-makara-and-the-plain?p=1453869#post1453869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ok, am i the only one who sees one of those right wing nuts who buy trumps lies as an archtypical example of the plain?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Plain can spawn of any political stance, as I see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-30T15:48:04-07:00","id":1453872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1452221-the-makara-and-the-plain?p=1453871#post1453871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Plain can spawn of any political stance, as I see it.</div> </div> </div> </div>sadly, you are right.<br /> <br /> i think that the Plain flock to fanatics and zealots like flies do to honey. the Plain's whole thing is &quot;this is the way the world works&quot; and ignoring the simple fact that it does not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-30T15:50:21-07:00","id":1453873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1452221-the-makara-and-the-plain?p=1453871#post1453871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Plain can spawn of any political stance, as I see it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is correct.<br /> <br /> Which isn't to say I <i>wasn't</i> thinking about the American conservative voting blocs at the time of the writing (&quot;the common clay of the new west&quot;), but any political ideology can have someone reduce the world to that view. Again, the ground work is a personal one, which is always polticially influenced but not always politically acted upon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-30T18:05:44-07:00","id":1453880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1452221-the-makara-and-the-plain?p=1453873#post1453873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is correct.<br /> <br /> Which isn't to say I <i>wasn't</i> thinking about the American conservative voting blocs at the time of the writing (&quot;the common clay of the new west&quot;), but any political ideology can have someone reduce the world to that view. Again, the ground work is a personal one, which is always polticially influenced but not always politically acted upon.</div> </div> </div> </div>thanks for confirming that the plain are made from the zealots and fanatics of the world. those that can not be reasoned with. its a sad truth that fanatics like how the plain are described can not be stopped even if there god appeared in front of them and said they were wrong and to stop being stupid. it aint just limited to trump supporters, as sadly any idealogy can become horribly twisted and used for evil. i mean islamic terrorists basically twist a single line of there own holy scriptures to cast off there non violent faith. <br /> <br /> its sad that humanity can twist what was meant to be good into the worst of the worst.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-30T21:03:07-07:00","id":1453887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1452221-the-makara-and-the-plain?p=1453880#post1453880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> thanks for confirming that the plain are made from the zealots and fanatics of the world. those that can not be reasoned with. its a sad truth that fanatics like how the plain are described can not be stopped even if there god appeared in front of them and said they were wrong and to stop being stupid. it aint just limited to trump supporters, as sadly any idealogy can become horribly twisted and used for evil. i mean islamic terrorists basically twist a single line of there own holy scriptures to cast off there non violent faith.<br /> <br /> its sad that humanity can twist what was meant to be good into the worst of the worst.</div> </div> </div> </div>No fault or statement on you, but I feel I must point out an irony, that this makes me ruminate on, that exists on this thread that doesn't exist in the other two, one that is delicious and bitter:<br /> <br /> <i>It's not that simple</i>.<br /> <br /> The Plain stick primarily to what they know and fight in advocation for it. And in the modern political climate, with ultranationalistic authoritarianism on the rise globablly and some very violent reactions in response societally (Like ISIS)*, it's very easy to point at the Plain (and a lot of the other Heroic Forswearings) as being the sort of the people who are the problem(and some of them are more than others-coming around to the Immortal in a pre-post-Covid-19 world is <i>interesting)</i>-and there's a lot of truth there, let's not sugarcoat it. And it would be wonderful if we could keep it that reductive at all points and times as it goes. Wouldn't it be great if we could just say the Plain are awful?<br /> <br /> And not responsible for some eye opening things, like, say, <a href=\"https://www.naturalhistorymag.com/picks-from-the-past/12476/shakespeare-in-the-bush\" target=\"_blank\">Shakespeare in the Bush?</a><br /> <br /> (For context, Shakespeare in the Bush is an article about how people removed from the wider constructs that Shakespeare relies on have a wildly different take, and actually teach how Shakespeare doesn't work in all circumstances-which in and of itself speaks to a new and fuller understanding of what it takes to construct the human. It's a wonderful argument, and the revelations that emerges from one reductive stance challenging another is phenomenal, and one the <i>Makara</i> could not ever make.)<br /> <br /> When colonialist powers roll into an area and attempt to stamp out a culture, the Plain are the ones who fight to preserve that culture. When capitalist powers try to turn everything into a complicated argument how things will benefit everyone in the long term, it's the Plain who drag the argument to how industrial attitudes hurt the people here and now. When assholes try to drag in truly harmful deviant sexual identities like pedophilia into fights about sexual social liberty, it's the Plain who cut the line between actual harm and the flimsier understandings of what harm is-the Makara can help explain finer nuances of it all, but Plain <i>make the point</i>.<br /> <br /> THe Makara embody alien worlds that exist under the surface, and I can point towards both sex, sexuality, and gender orientation as one point where it's scary to dive in and where some people will just say &quot;No, it's simpler than you're trying to make it.&quot;, <i>and </i>to <i>live-action roleplaying</i>, how many variations of LARPing exist and just how many people <i>actually</i> engage with it-and I have actually scared people off who were interested by letting my overcomplicated mind try and explain that, much to my regret.<br /> <br /> By contrast, the Plain are tradition keepers and culture greeters. They're the sort of people for whom the cutting of the Gordian is not some grandiose philosophical statement of Occam's Razor but just how you deal with troublesome knots. They're the sort of people who think you'll get line dancing or the Awa Dance Festival if you would just shut up about cultural value and <i>fucking do it</i>.<br /> <br /> Like, they are the &quot;common clay of the west, you know, morons&quot;, but they are also the sort of people who write diaries about their time because one day it'll disappear and people need to know about it. The fact that these future makers are wrong has no bearing on the fact that we would still be so much more greatly enriched if the Irish or the Norse had <i>fucking written down their fucking mythologies before Christianization</i>.**<br /> <br /> Like, I don't ever want to lose sight of the fact that <i>rejecting fear</i> is toxic as fucking hell, don't get me wrong, but these guys <i>are</i> Heroes for unironic reasons as much as there are <i>ironic</i> ones. They <i>can</i>, and often <i>do</i> contribute to many good things, things we in our modern era would fight for.<br /> <br /> Beast <i>should</i> flip the script and point out the problems with the average mentality, but it would be a shallow game if Beasts just made good points and Heroes <i>didn't</i> make good points, or have their mindsets contribute to their societies. Beast is a game about terrible people making good points that can either justify <i>why</i> they're there or <i>cover </i>for the fact that they're terrible.<br /> <br /> The Makara are the embodiment that nothing's easy to understand*** and that there's a whole fucking lot to understand-borrowing a little bit from an earlier comment, the Makara are the fear of just <i>how much</i> there is to learn and how it can feeling <i>drowning</i>, how it can feel like a <i>fight for air</i> to comprehend the self and the world-but the Plain are valuable because they allow for <i>foundations</i> to learn from.<br /> <br /> Don't ever assume things are easy when discussing the depths-it's always a little bit deeper than you think. Unless, of course, things really are that simple. Take the dive, but don't go in head-first.<br /> <br /> *in a way that makes the Hegemony Ministry <i>cackle</i>.<br /> **I am bitter, yes.<br /> ***and listen, as someone who has made some of the dive to realize myself as a gender fluid, pre-trans-op feminine sexed, and kind of still figuring out what the fuck my sexuality is, compared to the boy started from being a <i>Mormon</i>, a religious sect with <i>heavily</i> codified understandings of sex, gender, and sexuality, I want people to understand I <i>really</i> understand both where the Makara and the Plain are coming from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-30T21:32:29-07:00","id":1453888,"title":"","content":"And on record, I don't want people to overextend that into it's own false absolutist moral equivalency-there's absolutely things to draw lines about and say no to-Beast may be a game about playing monsters, and even having fun being a monster, and <i>definitely</i> questions being a monster, but it's not a fucking game that should say &quot;Yeah, yer okay for being a pedohpile/white supremacist/&quot;incel&quot;/etc.&quot; It's here to say monstrous behavior and actions come from some place, and that for people who can learn and grow from that place, chances should at least be perceivable-and for those who can't, Kinship should bow to Hunger as the leader of actions. And yes, Beast should be willing to say there is a line to things like this, even if it takes the long way around to draw.<br /> <br /> THese games should be cathartically transgressive, not supportive or foundational for actual monstrosity. Borderlands 2, not Hatred.<br /> <br /> That may be the Nemesis (and alcohol) in me speaking, but fuck it, I stand by it. There is a certain amount of toxicity that can be turned around, and there are absolute levels where it <i>can't</i>. Beast should at least feel out that line and try to stand on the right side of it at all times, even while it's having fun being a something of a shithead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-30T21:39:33-07:00","id":1453889,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I guess I was overgeneralizing. Its sadly very easy to do. <br /> <br /> And that is what makes the heroes work. They take the easy way, ie the bright turn on the lights instead of growing able to tolerate the dark, and the victorious refuse to belive in there own limits or those of others. They take the easy path instead of the one that allows you to grow as a person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","user":"evtrax","date":". 07-01-2021, 12:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-30T21:49:37-07:00","id":1453890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1452221-the-makara-and-the-plain?p=1453889#post1453889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. I guess I was overgeneralizing.</div> </div> </div> </div>TO be perfectly fair, it's a thing to happen.<br /> <br /> We're human. We're not omniscient and omnicomprehescient entities. We rely on consolidating and confining information in order to make sense of things. This is why the Makara are terrifying to us-because it presents a whole and terrifying alien world to understand, where we struggle to <i>breathe</i>. It's why the Plain are comforting-we can always rely on bringing the complicated down to simple principles.<br /> <br /> But again, Beast is a game that challenges our comforts. It points out how the Plain can become suffocating in their own right, particularly when allowed to be extreme. It can be transcendantal in helping us realize that learning more and growing our boxes, through the Makara<i>, </i>can not only help us handle more, but subject us to whole new delights and ways to be, that we can be <i>alien</i> in our own ways.<br /> <br /> Beast is....actually, shockingly simple in this way. Not <i>comfortably so</i>, but principle-y so. It's good guidelines to go and explore, challenge, learn, grow, and return--or-deviate as neccesary.<br /> <br /> THis game is about Transgression, and it's about Compassion. it is applied to self and to other, ands asks the weird question of what happens when a thing is <i>both</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T01:35:21-07:00","id":1453903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1452221-the-makara-and-the-plain?p=1453887#post1453887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>It's not that simple</i>.<br /> (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that my posts come in in fits and spurts, which makes it difficult to have a meaningful interplay with me, but I see this entire post as reassurance for my worries from the Anakim thread.<br /> <br /> *Chef's kiss*<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T07:50:30-07:00","id":1453933,"title":"","content":"Y\u2019know, I like these threads. And I also like B:tP, philosophy, and a fair bit of fiction and music. And you know what I\u2019ve learnt? It is that Wisdom can be found practically almost anywhere.<br /> <br /> Heck, <i>you</i>, ArcaneArts, are actually providing some legitimate wisdom in my eyes, whether you realise it or not.<br /> <br /> That Wisdom? It is thus; \u201cTo <b><i><u>truly</u></i></b> conquer fear, you must both accept it into yourself, and yet work against it.\u201d<br /> <br /> Your explanation of the Makara and Plain is a great example; things are complicated, and hard to understand, and can get absolutely messy, but it is still entirely possible to eventually come to <i>understand</i> them. But it is unwise to do so immediately, to attempt to understand something without trying to build a simple foundation on which to base said understanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-03T17:50:47-07:00","id":1454164,"title":"","content":"Arc,do you have any thoughts on the Incarnate? Any changee you want to make to them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-04T05:26:52-07:00","id":1454191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1452221-the-makara-and-the-plain?p=1454164#post1454164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arc,do you have any thoughts on the Incarnate? Any changee you want to make to them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean the Insatiable? Because the incarnation is an inheritance, aka an end game. The Insatiable are the primal nightmares, children of typhon instead of the dark mother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-04T07:48:28-07:00","id":1454202,"title":"","content":"I actually do mean the incarnate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-05T05:58:56-07:00","id":1454275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1452221-the-makara-and-the-plain?p=1454202#post1454202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually do mean the incarnate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. I would like to see the end games. But I would prefer to sew the Insatiable","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-05T10:10:53-07:00","id":1454288,"title":"","content":"The Insatiable are actually fairly simple, and once I get a Hunger write up to explain my thought process going into Chapter 1 of the Beast book, you'll see what I mean. For now, I'll say I dunno how the Insatiable ended up feeling kinda messy and janky when the obvious role and purpose of the Insatiable was staring everyone in the face-but this may be because I keep my Beast-as-commentary-on-nihilism glasses at the ready.<br /> <br /> The Incarnates <i>are</i> something I need to get around to really kicking around, though properly squaring Heroes and the Astral and expanding Kinship will probably answer a lot of that. In the short, thematically, the Incarnates are tuned correctly*, we don't need to course correct the ideas that make them up. Where Incarnates become interesting is regarding the larger scale issue of Beast's power scale and relationship to the rest of the Chronicles, what that should be, what's &quot;gated&quot; behind the Incarnate Inheritance, and how that should play between the themes.<br /> <br /> I suppose a simpler way to put it is that if we take the phrase &quot;A god is just a monster you kneel to&quot; as one of those vitally important concepts for looking at Beast, then what does it mean when the Incarnate are <i>still</i> a &quot;step up&quot; from Beasthood? In my conception of future versions of Beast having a lot more involvement with Astral Gods, what does it mean when I immediately say the Incarnates are among them, but waffle on whether or not that means High Lair Beasts aren't?<br /> <br /> THe framework for answering that problem is, like a lot of things in Beast, inherently there-I just haven't gotten around to firming it up into realization. And it's something I could probably rant a fair bit about.<br /> <br /> *It's a metaphor for suicide and a parallel to heroism (though not in the vein of way we're approaching Heroes with the Forsworn, and that's <i>fine</i>), mythic apotheosis that leaves nothing but the most self-satisfied monster, and that's <i>not</i> strictly a good thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-05T12:10:58-07:00","id":1454292,"title":"","content":"Seeing what you do with the Insatiable will be interesting, as I've long felt that there is a (probably unintentional) fundamental hypocrisy in their conception, but at the same time they bring enough to the table to make the setting deeper and more complex in some potentially satisfying ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-05T12:21:39-07:00","id":1454294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1452221-the-makara-and-the-plain?p=1454292#post1454292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeing what you do with the Insatiable will be interesting, as I've long felt that there is a (probably unintentional) fundamental hypocrisy in their conception, but at the same time they bring enough to the table to make the setting deeper and more complex in some potentially satisfying ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>We'll make a post on it later today. It really is just &quot;give them a better core to connect all the pieces and clean up some of the messier mechanics&quot; though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-31T15:36:03-07:00","id":1455879,"title":"","content":"Two thoughts<br /> <br /> 1) Is there a connection between the Plain from Hurt Locker and the Plain Forsworn? Beyond the name, I see a similar sort of simplistic, dogmatic worldview at play possibly.<br /> <br /> 2) Do the Makara always have to be the Depths you plunged yourself into? Can they sometimes be the flood that brought the depths to you no matter how you ran? Or is the Flood Anakim? I just wonder about this because I was thinking about a potential new Family yesterday (as part of a discussion, but I was more listening to myself than engaging with the other participants' ideas sadly) that was the fear of &quot;Being Wrong&quot;. The fear that you had bad information, made bad logical connections, somehow strayed into territory that will get you hurt or worse. Whether it was just following the wrong person or outright sensory hallucinations, you fear that your guide, your senses, can't be trusted. In my conception at the time, I guess I'm just wondering it that idea is totally covered by this version of the Makara","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T08:49:32-07:00","id":1455936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1452221-the-makara-and-the-plain?p=1455879#post1455879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Is there a connection between the Plain from Hurt Locker and the Plain Forsworn? Beyond the name, I see a similar sort of simplistic, dogmatic worldview at play possibly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Not really. Hurt Locker-style Plain are normal people who've started to tap into powers based on Radical levels of Non-Violence/Pacifism, whereas the Plain described in this thread are a &quot;Homebrew&quot; type of Hero who've rejected a type of fear in a manner that has the potential to become <u><i><b>extremely</b></i></u> toxic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1452221-the-makara-and-the-plain?p=1455879#post1455879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Do the Makara always have to be the Depths you plunged yourself into? Can they sometimes be the flood that brought the depths to you no matter how you ran? Or is the Flood Anakim? I just wonder about this because I was thinking about a potential new Family yesterday (as part of a discussion, but I was more listening to myself than engaging with the other participants' ideas sadly) that was the fear of &quot;Being Wrong&quot;. The fear that you had bad information, made bad logical connections, somehow strayed into territory that will get you hurt or worse. Whether it was just following the wrong person or outright sensory hallucinations, you fear that your guide, your senses, can't be trusted. In my conception at the time, I guess I'm just wondering it that idea is totally covered by this version of the Makara</div> </div> </div> </div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">\u2026I'm n</span>ot entirely sure, actually. Yo', <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a>! Got anything to say 'bout 'dis stuff?</div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T19:05:42-07:00","id":1455980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1452221-the-makara-and-the-plain?p=1455879#post1455879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two thoughts<br /> <br /> 1) Is there a connection between the Plain from Hurt Locker and the Plain Forsworn? Beyond the name, I see a similar sort of simplistic, dogmatic worldview at play possibly.<br /> <br /> 2) Do the Makara always have to be the Depths you plunged yourself into? Can they sometimes be the flood that brought the depths to you no matter how you ran? Or is the Flood Anakim? I just wonder about this because I was thinking about a potential new Family yesterday (as part of a discussion, but I was more listening to myself than engaging with the other participants' ideas sadly) that was the fear of &quot;Being Wrong&quot;. The fear that you had bad information, made bad logical connections, somehow strayed into territory that will get you hurt or worse. Whether it was just following the wrong person or outright sensory hallucinations, you fear that your guide, your senses, can't be trusted. In my conception at the time, I guess I'm just wondering it that idea is totally covered by this version of the Makara</div> </div> </div> </div>1) No, though I DID cackle at the deliberateness of perpetuating Chronicles &quot;Demon, Demon, Demon&quot; problem in that way. But the Plain of Hurt Locker are generally kind of fucking amazing pacifists who actually are taking a pretty hard answer to a even harder question. The Plain, Heroes who Forswear the Depths, are people who keep from drowning by never swimming and will drown goldfish in the wide open fields for daring to do so.<br /> <br /> 2)I'd peg that Family idea more as the Inguma, Inguma as Fear of the Other extending beyond basic stranger danger and into the genuinely disquieting notion that other people know you better than you do and represent what you should be. A big reason people react negatively to the Other is that Others are statements of how to be-and if that person seems to be getting more form that state of being, it can easily read as though they're trying to tell you how to be.<br /> <br /> but hell, maybe you do, and you just have trouble admitting that to yourself.<br /> <br /> That said, the Fear the Makara CAN represent with that, though, is when a person realizes that what seemed like a simple and easy world they entered into is a lot more terrifying complex.....and oh gee, the surface is <i>so</i> far away. They could lose themselves and drown in this world, which might mean dying, or becoming a person they don't understand at all but feel they can no longer escape.<br /> <br /> Beast has always had some thin lines to cut and transition over-look at the way people have trouble reconciling the difference between the Anakim and the Talasii, or how there was once an argument that the Anakim represented every other family, or the confusion about the Eshmaki and the Makara in these threads. A lot of the time, it comes down to what, exactly, a person is really reacting to when they encounter something, and that can be hard to cut the difference between. It takes introspection and a lot of careful parsing out, the sort of things Beasts go through with their Devouring into enlighenment.<br /> <br /> EDIT: on the Flood, because I was really wanting to talk about that but missed it:<br /> <br /> It depends on the reaction to the Flood. if the fear is in trying to figure out how you're going ot get around town, where you're getting food from ,where you'll sleep, thinking you might be able swim across, but what about differing currents, or objects being swept along-like, you know you can hypothetically survive the flood because others have but you feel overwhelmed trying to figure out how <i>you're</i> going to do it, that's the Makara. If instead you're just crushed by the inability to do <i>anything</i> as the waters weep through and destroy your homes and hang out, carries away your pets faster than you can ever hope to swim and catch up, the certainty that you <i>can't</i> swim across that rapid-that there's nothing you can do about the flood, and your life is in the hands of more competent strangers and the water itself, that's a watery Anakim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-01-2021, 10:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T04:14:11-07:00","id":1456001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1452221-the-makara-and-the-plain?p=1455980#post1455980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) No, though I DID cackle at the deliberateness of perpetuating Chronicles &quot;Demon, Demon, Demon&quot; problem in that way. But the Plain of Hurt Locker are generally kind of fucking amazing pacifists who actually are taking a pretty hard answer to a even harder question. The Plain, Heroes who Forswear the Depths, are people who keep from drowning by never swimming and will drown goldfish in the wide open fields for daring to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pascifism, <b><i><u>FUCK YEAH!</u></i></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-04T15:30:24-07:00","id":1456152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1452221-the-makara-and-the-plain?p=1455980#post1455980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2)I'd peg that Family idea more as the Inguma, Inguma as Fear of the Other extending beyond basic stranger danger and into the genuinely disquieting notion that other people know you better than you do and represent what you should be. A big reason people react negatively to the Other is that Others are statements of how to be-and if that person seems to be getting more form that state of being, it can easily read as though they're trying to tell you how to be.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, the book is right. That *is* a very human-centric fear. Other animals hide and fight non-kin, but I can't really imagine even a dolphin fearing that they are doing &quot;being a dolphin&quot; wrong, even to deny it. The wild animal fears many, many things. But they know in their bones what they are, and what they are told by their very DNA to do in most relevant situations. And even when they have more subjective choices, like mates and a glut of food choices, they don't tend to look to other animals for that answer once they've left infancy.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Now I'm thinking back to my recent evolutionary biology/sociology of humanity class and wondering what Family would house the fear and lesson that we are our minds are just as bound by the evolutionary past as our bodies, but that but by understanding that past and what it means, we can create a world where humans can feel not just materially cared for (though we need to make that more universal too), but even spiritually fulfilled. I'm thinking Namtaru, for that acceptance of imperfection and your own body turning against you. The Horror would likely look like some filthy, blood-stained nightmare version of one of those early illustrations of neanderthals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 08-04-2021, 06:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-04T17:34:52-07:00","id":1456154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1452221-the-makara-and-the-plain?p=1456152#post1456152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh, the book is right. That *is* a very human-centric fear. Other animals hide and fight non-kin, but I can't really imagine even a dolphin fearing that they are doing &quot;being a dolphin&quot; wrong, even to deny it. The wild animal fears many, many things. But they know in their bones what they are, and what they are told by their very DNA to do in most relevant situations. And even when they have more subjective choices, like mates and a glut of food choices, they don't tend to look to other animals for that answer once they've left infancy.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Now I'm thinking back to my recent evolutionary biology/sociology of humanity class and wondering what Family would house the fear and lesson that we are our minds are just as bound by the evolutionary past as our bodies, but that but by understanding that past and what it means, we can create a world where humans can feel not just materially cared for (though we need to make that more universal too), but even spiritually fulfilled. I'm thinking Namtaru, for that acceptance of imperfection and your own body turning against you. The Horror would likely look like some filthy, blood-stained nightmare version of one of those early illustrations of neanderthals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Humans are social creatures, and the Inguma are rooted in that instinct to form and keep to groups contrasted with the fear that being in a group is to place yourself among wolves who might very eat their own.<br /> <br /> The fear that comes from realizing we're basically arrogant and self-deluded animals, walking biological computers whose precepts of free will are untroubling quirks to the protein-programs we're just executing can definitely trigger that failure of form the Namtaru embody-no matter how the ape tries to the meeting the falling angel, it too will fall back, because al it ever was was an ape-but it can also be a neat Talassii mentality, particularly if it crashes through a hunger for trans- or post-humanity, and on the grand scale existential despair it can end up being a Anakim fear as well.<br /> <br /> And it goes without saying that the terrrible, perpetual realization of that notion whille still being a slave to it makes the Insatiable <i>giddy</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-19T10:03:41-07:00","id":1493337,"title":"","content":"Heh. Under this conception, I think I like the Makara the most philosophically. I understand the fear of complexity and yearning for simple answers, while also trying to live by two maxims: &quot;Everything is complex on some level&quot; and &quot;If it looks like it's easy, it's because someone else did all the heavy lifting.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-22T13:03:06-07:00","id":1493531,"title":"","content":"Arc,what are the seven Hungers all about in your new take on Beast? Apologies if you already answered that one,i couldn't find it on my own","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-22T15:29:51-07:00","id":1493535,"title":"","content":"I think I have mentioned it before, but I don't think I've ever spelled it out in full.<br /> <br /> So, The world's a scary place, I think we've established that. All that is frightening in the world is, by it's very nature, scary and intimidating to confront, understand, and come to terms with, and no one expects anyone to just nail harmonization and equanimity with fear out of the case, to turn it into empathy and care and community just like <i>that</i>. It's a process, one that, by it's nature, requires one to pull back from time to time, to have a barrier between you and <i>it</i>. More over, not all incarnations of fear are harmless-indeed, many of them will chew you up and leave you for dead on the rocks. Heroes aren't wrong when they question the sanity of walking naked into a sandstorm or why you don't just turn on a light to get through the dark. Our basic survival is often met with food and drink, clothing, housing, and fuel for warmth, but when it comes to security in a world full of monsters, at some point, we all need our safety blankets beyond the basics.<br /> <br /> Hungers are those safety blankets-the hunger is for safety and security and comfort that comes from accruing power or collecting stuff or knowing all the secrets, being able to predate upon on others or know that you can ruin anything and burn any bridge, to rely upon a system of punishments or deftly transgress against such.<br /> <br /> Spend enough time divorced from fear, these Hungers mark a transition from simple desire for security into desire for itself, a thing that is collected because it fills you, it satisfies you, maybe even makes you happy, a thing that spirals into itself and shells outward into homes, communities, cities, nations-civilization itself. Go through any place in the world you would like, you can see how the stones of each are laid in pursuit of those Hungers-wise civilizations even understand that transgression is a needful thing, as law and order can be cloying and rotting things, and that a little freedom and challenge in the populace releases pressures that might otherwise stress, strain, and break a society (look at civilization's long and sometimes complicated relationship with alcohol).<br /> <br /> As a rule, as a general thing, it is understood as a good and meet thing to sate Hunger-we all need a measure of these things to be whole and secure in our own right, and to be wielded to foster and build it up for others. But it's one thing to sate, quite another to glut. If/When we do things like the family write ups for Hunger-if the key to Families is <i>and that's all right</i>, for Hunger it's <i>and that is all well and good.....up to a point</i>. Some will accrue their Hunger to an excessive amount, til they are divorced from genuine fear and their humanity, some will starve others of their Hungers. Beasts will sometimes pick targets because their abundance of Satiety is leading them to mute their psychospiritual senses and connections, sometimes they'll go after someone because they're being an asshole in pursuit or success with their Hunger.....or sometimes because they just want it.<br /> <br /> The Three Main Sections I'd have in a new core would be something like To Take And Waste (since at a minimum every Beast must take the representation of someone's Hunger to sate their own, and the closest kin to that is to destroy it), To Keep and Build (since a lot of Beasts will of course incorproate their gains into their Lives and Lairs, and build from there), and To Return and Gift (because sometimes, the point is that someone just needs to remember what it was like without the blanket, and thus a Beast can give it back after the fact, or otherwise gift it to worthier, wiser people-or just whoever they want to).<br /> <br /> The Insatiable have the clearest relationship to Hunger, namely in that in their over-satiation, they demonstrate the folly of trying to divorce away from fear, and with it the world and the animal self-that no amount of Satiation can <i>actually</i> make you safe, secure, comfortable. Heroes contrast that, and almost prove the Insatiable's point-in that, since they have such an abundance of Hunger and it's Satiation, how could any think they're afraid, putting the cart before the horse and presenting persona as self.<br /> <br /> But yeah, the tl;dr of it all is &quot;If Family is Fear, Hunger is Security&quot;. Hunger is the reason Beasts have just as much in common with the Spring Court as they do the Autumn Court.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-22-2022, 11:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-22T20:10:46-07:00","id":1493554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_co